{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Legally mandate premium holiday pay for all hospitality workers",
        "additional_details": "Unlike many sectors, the hospitality industry experiences its highest demand during bank holidays. Workers are routinely required to sacrifice time with their families, friends & communities to keep the economy running, yet the current law does not guarantee them a penny of extra pay for doing so. Under current employment law, there is no statutory right to extra pay on bank holidays; it is entirely at the employer's discretion. This can leave low-paid workers vulnerable to burnout & unfair compensation. As part of the Government's commitment to \"Make Work Pay\" and the introduction of the Employment Rights Act, a mandatory premium rate for holiday shifts should be codified into law. We believe hospitality workers deserve fair compensation for giving up their holidays to serve others.",
        "background": "We call on the Government to introduce legislation that legally entitles all hospitality workers to a mandatory premium pay rate (minimum time-and-a-half) or guaranteed paid time off in lieu for working on official UK Bank Holidays.",
